1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,433
<i> We can beat them.</i>

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:05,300
<i>Joey, who is your boyfriend
or suitor?</i>

3
00:00:05,433 --> 00:00:08,167
<i>Oh, no. Those three are really
competitive.</i>

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,233
<i> And they're working out.</i>

5
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:10,533
<i>They're showing off
their physiques.</i>

6
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:11,400
<i> Don't look at them!</i>

7
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:12,767
<i> Joey, I have a question.</i>

8
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,400
<i>So among the three of us,
who has the best body?</i>

9
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:17,933
<i>That's right,
it should be like that,</i>

10
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:19,300
<i>and not fighting
with each other,</i>

11
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:21,633
<i>and taking your clothes off.
It's embarrassing for the kids.</i>

12
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:22,700
<i> I'm sorry.</i>

13
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:25,367
<i>We promised them
that we would do our best.</i>

14
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,067
<i>Well, I'm happy that we're on
the same side today</i>

15
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,867
<i>because I'm not used to being on
the same side.</i>

16
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,267
<i>And you're happier
when I'm by your side...</i>

17
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:35,700
<i> I mean, the three of us.</i>

18
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:38,500
<i>You know, because you were so
focused on being so competitive,</i>

19
00:00:38,633 --> 00:00:39,967
<i> the kid got hurt.</i>

20
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,567
<i> When luck is on our side,</i>

21
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:42,967
<i>both mother and daughter
are together.</i>

22
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:43,833
<i> Someone's coming, Boss.</i>

23
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:44,900
<i> Let's leave.</i>

24
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,033
<i>The other guy is Berdugo's
brother-in-law.</i>

25
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:47,400
<i> He can't see me.</i>

26
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:48,633
<i>- Hey!
- Hey...</i>

27
00:00:48,767 --> 00:00:51,633
<i>Could it be that my daughter
and I are their targets?</i>

28
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:55,000
<i>Maybe this is related
to my husband's case.</i>

29
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,800
<i> This is kind of weird for me.</i>

30
00:00:56,933 --> 00:00:58,933
<i>I'm not used to having friends.</i>

31
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:02,600
<i>You know, it's hard to find real
friends.</i>

32
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:05,633
<i>That's why we should take care
of our friendship, right?</i>

33
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:06,733
<i> Theresa...</i>

34
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,600
<i>It's not just about me and you.</i>

35
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:10,433
<i> I have to protect my friends.</i>

36
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:12,233
<i> I have to protect Joey.</i>

37
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:13,567
<i> Sorry, Miss Delgado.</i>

38
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:16,300
<i>The court did not accept
the witness statement</i>

39
00:01:16,433 --> 00:01:18,000
<i> due to technicalities.</i>

40
00:01:18,133 --> 00:01:19,200
<i> What?</i>

41
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,467
Buddy,

42
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,767
I heard you have a new witness
in your case.

43
00:01:52,067 --> 00:01:54,133
Where did you hear that?

44
00:01:54,267 --> 00:01:57,100
We have a saying here inside.

45
00:01:57,233 --> 00:02:01,100
The news outside seeps through
the bars.

46
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:03,433
What? Do you have a big chance?

47
00:02:03,567 --> 00:02:06,000
Or maybe you've been acquitted?

48
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:08,367
You don't need the information
you asked me

49
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,167
for about Berdugo anymore.

50
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,000
I still need it.

51
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,700
You really still plan
to clash with Berdugo's group

52
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:21,000
even though you're free.

53
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:23,100
I don't know if there's
something really wrong

54
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:25,100
with your head.

55
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:27,800
I'll decide what to do
with that information.

56
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:30,533
What?

57
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:34,233
Will you keep your promise
or not?

58
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,233
I have one word.

59
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:39,667
I don't have the
information right now,

60
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,933
but I'll give it to you.

61
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:43,200
If I were you, I'd hurry up
with your coffee there.

62
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:44,800
The jail guard is coming.

63
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:47,667
Where is it?

64
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,433
Because there is no supporting
evidence,

65
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:59,567
everything Golda said in court
was considered hearsay.

66
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:03,867
So, what now?

67
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,200
Well, maybe the decision could
be changed

68
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:07,833
if we talk to the judge.

69
00:03:09,533 --> 00:03:12,333
Joey, I don't think we can do
that at this point.

70
00:03:12,467 --> 00:03:16,267
Actually, I think someone
already talked to the judge,

71
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,267
which is why he made
the decision that way.

72
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,000
Maybe someone sabotaged
our case.

73
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:26,567
It's Berdugo.

74
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:29,333
His connections are really wide,
Joey.

75
00:03:29,467 --> 00:03:31,333
We can't beat him.

76
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:33,667
So...

77
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,800
What now? Nothing?
That's just gone?

78
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:39,333
Is it over?
There's nothing we can do?

79
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,433
If Golda's statement
can't be used,

80
00:03:42,567 --> 00:03:43,833
how can Father be free?

81
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:46,200
What are we going to do, Andrew?

82
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:48,100
Everything we worked hard for...

83
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:49,933
everything we worked hard for,
is gone?

84
00:03:56,133 --> 00:03:57,100
Joey...

85
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,067
Hello, Mother?

86
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:11,267
Have you heard about father's
case?

87
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:15,100
I talked to the attorney
earlier, Joey.

88
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:17,133
<i> I already know what happened.</i>

89
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,000
Why is this happening to us,
Mom?

90
00:04:24,033 --> 00:04:25,900
We looked for Golda
for a long time.

91
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:28,333
I've been going through so much
just to get her to testify,

92
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,033
and then they'll just
throw it away.

93
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:34,133
What's that?
All my sacrifices are gone?

94
00:04:34,267 --> 00:04:36,833
It's not like that, Joey.

95
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:42,900
If it weren't for what you did,
I wouldn't know the truth.

96
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:48,133
That Golda and your Father
didn't have an affair.

97
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:50,533
But, Mother, what about Father
now?

98
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:52,833
We have no way out of his case.

99
00:04:52,967 --> 00:04:55,467
Joey, don't lose hope.

100
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,967
<i> God has mercy.</i>

101
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:01,933
I also believe that.

102
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,967
He listens to our prayers.

103
00:05:06,533 --> 00:05:08,567
<i> Our family will be reunited.</i>

104
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:11,700
<i> It will happen.</i>

105
00:05:13,133 --> 00:05:15,800
So just hold on, my child, okay?

106
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:24,433
So that's Berdugo's plan.

107
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,367
To bribe the judge.

108
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,800
That's great.

109
00:05:27,933 --> 00:05:29,667
Everything has a price.

110
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,367
You just need to know how much.

111
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:37,633
Well, at least Berdugo is happy.

112
00:05:37,767 --> 00:05:40,000
Delgado will have nothing
to look forward to,

113
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:42,300
and his case will have
no way out,

114
00:05:42,433 --> 00:05:45,033
and he'll rot in jail.

115
00:05:45,167 --> 00:05:46,567
Exactly!

116
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:06,267
Joey?

117
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:09,467
What are you doing?

118
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,367
Researching.

119
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,667
Researching...

120
00:06:18,133 --> 00:06:19,700
Wait, did you sleep yet?

121
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:25,933
Now that Golda's testimony
is no longer valid,

122
00:06:26,067 --> 00:06:28,833
I need to find another strategy
to help my father.

123
00:06:30,367 --> 00:06:32,800
I understand where you're coming
from, Joey.

124
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:35,400
I know you really want
to help your father.

125
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,933
But you should know that
he has an attorney,

126
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,367
and he knows what to do.

127
00:06:46,033 --> 00:06:48,167
Andrew, it's hard to hope again.

128
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:53,167
What if father's attorney
doesn't have a defense?

129
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:59,000
You know, I'm so confused
just thinking about it.

130
00:07:00,933 --> 00:07:03,767
I don't know what to do
to help my father.

131
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,600
Honestly, I'm really
having a hard time, Andrew.

132
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:20,500
I just really want to help Joey.

133
00:07:20,633 --> 00:07:22,367
But how, Boss?

134
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,633
You did everything already.

135
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:27,200
You're so involved in that case.

136
00:07:28,733 --> 00:07:29,800
I know,

137
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:37,467
but I can't just back out,
right?

138
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,600
You know, honestly,

139
00:07:38,733 --> 00:07:41,767
I feel like a miracle is all
that will help me...

140
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,633
unless you have a suggestion.

141
00:07:45,467 --> 00:07:50,733
Guys! Guys! Stop talking.
Listen to what I have to say.

142
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:53,200
No one is talking here.

143
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:54,300
You spoke.

144
00:07:54,433 --> 00:07:55,967
No, this is more important.

145
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,700
Go ahead. Go, what's that?

146
00:07:57,833 --> 00:08:00,300
My vlogger friend texted.

147
00:08:00,433 --> 00:08:03,767
There's a big scoop,
as in a really big one.

148
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,433
But now, we need to go
to Bolagos Lake.

149
00:08:06,567 --> 00:08:09,067
Wait, why are we going
to Bolagos?

150
00:08:22,467 --> 00:08:23,900
That's a lot.

151
00:08:25,667 --> 00:08:27,267
Sir, who saw that?

152
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,533
They said it was divers
who were vlogging.

153
00:08:30,667 --> 00:08:32,600
They're giving statements
at the precinct.

154
00:08:32,733 --> 00:08:34,067
With so many of them,

155
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:37,067
we suspect that these people
are victims of a syndicate.

156
00:08:44,167 --> 00:08:45,733
This is the diver vloggers'
first time

157
00:08:45,867 --> 00:08:47,233
visiting Bolagos Lake.

158
00:08:47,367 --> 00:08:49,433
The vloggers' intention
was to provide entertaining

159
00:08:49,567 --> 00:08:50,733
and educational content,

160
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:55,033
but what surprised them
was a disgusting sight.

161
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,100
According to the police,

162
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:58,033
additional weights were placed
in the bags

163
00:08:58,167 --> 00:09:00,900
containing the bodies so that
they would not rise and float.

164
00:09:01,033 --> 00:09:05,200
This is just an example,
not the actual bag.

165
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:08,767
<i>The Bolagos Police promise
to identify the bodies found</i>

166
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:11,067
<i>and find out what really
happened to them</i>

167
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:14,200
<i>and who should be held
responsible for the deaths</i>

168
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:17,200
<i> of the victims.</i>

169
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:20,000
Only a demon would do that.

170
00:09:20,133 --> 00:09:23,000
The victims and their families
are pitiful.

171
00:09:32,133 --> 00:09:33,567
Have a drink first.

172
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:37,433
Did you see it, Mom?

173
00:09:37,567 --> 00:09:39,900
The bodies are in the bag.

174
00:09:40,033 --> 00:09:42,867
We saw it on social media.

175
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,633
That's terrible, Hon.
It's horrifying!

176
00:09:45,767 --> 00:09:47,467
Who would've thought that
it could happen here?

177
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,133
It's so near us!

178
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:52,167
I mean, I thought we were safe
in this place.

179
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:57,300
Do we need to be careful
of the people around us?

180
00:09:57,433 --> 00:09:58,567
Will you stop it?

181
00:09:59,633 --> 00:10:01,200
You're scaring the kids.

182
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,633
I don't want to talk about
those kinds of stories,

183
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:09,833
especially at the dinner table.
Understood?

184
00:10:09,967 --> 00:10:11,300
- Yes.
- Yes, Dad.

185
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,167
Come on.

186
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,633
Let's just eat.

187
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:30,833
We're trending!

188
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,600
There, Tirada is back
on top again.

189
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:35,700
It's a good thing

190
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:38,367
you were the first to come up
with this scoop.

191
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:43,267
No, of course, thanks to Kyle
and his friend, right?

192
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:46,200
I may be the one in front
of the screen,

193
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:48,567
but we all deserve the credit.

194
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:50,767
<i> Great.</i>

195
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:54,067
I think Berdugo's group
did that.

196
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:56,800
Because I remember before

197
00:10:56,933 --> 00:10:58,767
that when someone collided
with Berdugo,

198
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,600
he would suddenly disappear.

199
00:11:02,933 --> 00:11:04,167
Are you sure?

200
00:11:05,467 --> 00:11:06,433
Yes.

201
00:11:12,467 --> 00:11:13,833
Are you okay, Boss?

202
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:19,233
I was just thinking about
our report earlier.

203
00:11:19,367 --> 00:11:25,100
I mean, which God has
the right to say,

204
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:29,667
to decide when a person
will die?

205
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:33,333
He just threw away the
victims like garbage, right?

206
00:11:33,467 --> 00:11:37,633
As if the victim had no
personality, dreams, or family.

207
00:11:39,267 --> 00:11:41,667
The person who did this
must have thought

208
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:43,800
that the bodies would never
be found.

209
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:49,067
There is no secret that goes
undiscovered.

210
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:52,433
That's why I think
that if Berdugo catches me,

211
00:11:52,567 --> 00:11:56,300
that's definitely what
I'll end up with.

212
00:11:56,433 --> 00:11:59,367
They'll torture me, kill me...

213
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,267
They'll put me in a bag,

214
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,467
then suddenly they'll dump me
somewhere.

215
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,200
Where no one can find me.

216
00:12:05,333 --> 00:12:07,633
No trace. Not even a shadow
of me, nothing.

217
00:12:08,733 --> 00:12:10,167
Just like what happened
to Godfather Diego.

218
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,800
He just disappeared all
of a sudden.

219
00:12:11,933 --> 00:12:14,467
No one escapes from Berdugo.

220
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,333
He's that cruel.

221
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,400
You mean,

222
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:24,133
it's possible that one
of the bodies found

223
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:25,700
belongs to Godfather Diego?

224
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:34,733
It will eventually come out.

225
00:12:34,867 --> 00:12:40,033
Whoever is behind this,
in our next report,

226
00:12:40,167 --> 00:12:43,100
the hashtag we'll use
is "DemonyoReveal".

227
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,067
How did this happen?

228
00:12:49,233 --> 00:12:51,933
There are celebrity vloggers
diving and found the corpses.

229
00:12:52,067 --> 00:12:55,300
Don't worry,
I'll make them suffer.

230
00:12:56,333 --> 00:12:57,500
Stupid!

231
00:12:57,633 --> 00:12:59,533
The news will get hotter.

232
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:02,967
It'll get more attention.

233
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,500
<i> I'm sorry, Boss.</i>

234
00:13:04,633 --> 00:13:06,433
But what are we going to do?

235
00:13:06,567 --> 00:13:08,200
Should we just let them be?

236
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:10,300
We have no choice.

237
00:13:10,433 --> 00:13:13,833
What you have to make sure
of is that those corpses

238
00:13:13,967 --> 00:13:16,433
can't be connected to us.

239
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:18,200
It won't, Boss.

240
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:21,433
They definitely won't find
anything on those bodies.

241
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,067
<i> You're being arrogant.</i>

242
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,933
If this comes back to me,

243
00:13:25,067 --> 00:13:27,500
I'll have someone throw you
next.

244
00:13:37,467 --> 00:13:39,767
I told you,
I'll take care of it.

245
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:41,533
I'll take care of it.

246
00:13:41,667 --> 00:13:44,500
You really bought a lot.

247
00:13:44,633 --> 00:13:48,233
And then, you spent a lot.
And you didn't report for work.

248
00:13:49,833 --> 00:13:52,667
What's with you? I'm fine.
I'm on call.

249
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:56,533
Besides, Uncle will call me if
he needs me to do something.

250
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:59,700
And I won't leave you alone,
if you're not okay.

251
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:03,067
Thank you.

252
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:10,500
Good move.

253
00:14:10,633 --> 00:14:13,133
At least, now, Andrew
is not overshadowing you.

254
00:14:13,267 --> 00:14:14,367
Joey?

255
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,333
Where is Joey?

256
00:14:15,467 --> 00:14:16,667
Andrew, why?

257
00:14:18,033 --> 00:14:20,633
Joey, I went home as soon
as I found this out.

258
00:14:20,767 --> 00:14:22,867
One of the bodies
has been identified

259
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,467
through dental records.

260
00:14:26,567 --> 00:14:30,767
And, Joey, it's Major Aglipay.
It's confirmed.

261
00:14:46,933 --> 00:14:48,200
Godfather?

262
00:14:56,467 --> 00:15:01,800
<i>Joey, no matter what happens,
don't go out, don't scream.</i>

263
00:15:01,967 --> 00:15:03,300
<i> Go away now.</i>

264
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,300
<i> Theresa...</i>

265
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:14,767
<i> How did you meet this Lisa?</i>

266
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,067
<i> Online.</i>

267
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,800
<i> We matched profiles.</i>

268
00:16:17,933 --> 00:16:21,067
<i>I messaged her, and she replied.</i>

269
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,933
<i> Give me your phone!</i>

270
00:16:22,067 --> 00:16:23,100
<i> Here.</i>

271
00:16:33,333 --> 00:16:34,833
Hey, what do you want?

272
00:16:34,967 --> 00:16:36,933
Are you still going to catch
Theresa?

273
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,100
Yes.

274
00:16:39,233 --> 00:16:43,800
I saw a deactivated account
that links to Theresa.

275
00:16:43,967 --> 00:16:47,667
I just need to pinpoint
the location of the IP address.

276
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:52,000
Then I'm sure that I will find
her there.

277
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:54,367
I just need to get my things.

278
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,133
So you're going to go home
to get it?

279
00:16:56,267 --> 00:16:57,567
I'll go home with you.
I'll help you.

280
00:16:57,700 --> 00:17:00,267
Aren't you supposed
to be with Joey?

281
00:17:04,067 --> 00:17:07,200
Joey doesn't need me anymore.

282
00:17:08,867 --> 00:17:10,700
Joey is with Andrew.

283
00:17:17,833 --> 00:17:19,333
Meow!

284
00:17:21,433 --> 00:17:23,767
Why did you meow? What was that?

285
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,133
Nothing. You know...

286
00:17:26,267 --> 00:17:29,500
I just saw the video.

287
00:17:30,533 --> 00:17:32,267
The sad boy like you.

288
00:17:33,633 --> 00:17:34,867
Sad boy?

289
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:42,933
You know, because you've never
ever felt what I felt here.

290
00:17:43,067 --> 00:17:44,367
What makes you say that?

291
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,300
Don't you know what I've been
through?

292
00:17:47,467 --> 00:17:49,300
Okay. Fine, tell me.

293
00:17:49,467 --> 00:17:51,000
Tell me what you've been
through.

294
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:54,233
Maybe next time.

295
00:17:54,367 --> 00:17:56,600
Just go to Joey.

296
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:58,133
Go, Brother!

297
00:18:20,367 --> 00:18:22,067
You know, Joey,

298
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,400
I know your Godfather Diego.

299
00:18:28,267 --> 00:18:29,333
To this day,

300
00:18:29,467 --> 00:18:33,900
I can't believe he was involved
in that syndicate.

301
00:18:35,267 --> 00:18:36,900
Me too, Mom.

302
00:18:38,833 --> 00:18:41,933
Even though Godfather Diego
wronged us,

303
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:44,767
he still didn't deserve
what happened to him.

304
00:18:47,233 --> 00:18:52,233
I just hope he had at least a
little time to repent

305
00:18:52,367 --> 00:18:54,033
and change his life.

306
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:16,000
Our contact at the precinct
said that the ashes

307
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:18,733
and Parak's belongings
were given to relatives.

308
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,533
What?

309
00:19:20,667 --> 00:19:23,400
What we paid those idiots
is wasted

310
00:19:23,533 --> 00:19:26,000
if they couldn't follow simple
orders.

311
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:28,900
All the belongings were checked
before they were released,

312
00:19:29,067 --> 00:19:30,433
so they're safe.

313
00:19:30,567 --> 00:19:32,267
<i> That's not enough.</i>

314
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:36,167
You have so many loose ends like
that Golda case.

315
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:40,333
You thought she was dead,
but she was still able to talk.

316
00:19:40,467 --> 00:19:42,167
We have to make sure Parak

317
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:44,767
didn't leave anything else
behind.

318
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,900
If you need to find where
his belongings were taken,

319
00:19:49,033 --> 00:19:50,933
that's what you do.

320
00:19:51,067 --> 00:19:52,467
Mrs. Delgado,

321
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:55,633
as you and Miguel are listed
next of kin to Diego,

322
00:19:55,767 --> 00:19:58,600
Major Aglipay's remains
will go to you,

323
00:19:58,733 --> 00:20:01,300
as well as his office
belongings.

324
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:04,933
The entire police force
sympathizes with you.

325
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:08,433
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

326
00:20:08,567 --> 00:20:09,900
Please sit down.

327
00:20:10,033 --> 00:20:11,700
- We'll put this away.
- Thank you.

328
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,633
I'll just put this on the altar,
okay?

329
00:21:04,767 --> 00:21:06,100
We're working on it, Berdugo.

330
00:21:06,933 --> 00:21:09,200
But just a thought...

331
00:21:09,367 --> 00:21:11,100
since Diego has no family,

332
00:21:11,333 --> 00:21:13,433
The next of kin are most likely
the Delgados.

333
00:21:13,567 --> 00:21:16,700
<i>Probably, Delgado's wife already
has the things.</i>

334
00:21:16,833 --> 00:21:18,367
Well, in that case,

335
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:23,067
I'll take care of it so I don't
hear any more failures.

336
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,400
Everything okay?

337
00:21:45,533 --> 00:21:46,833
Yes.

338
00:21:46,967 --> 00:21:50,100
I just remembered what you
told me

339
00:21:50,233 --> 00:21:53,400
about our employee asking
for help.

340
00:21:53,533 --> 00:21:57,567
It's slipped from my mind,
but I do want to help.

341
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,233
Clarissa?

342
00:21:59,367 --> 00:22:00,433
Yes.

343
00:22:00,567 --> 00:22:02,600
I want to meet her as soon
as possible.

344
00:22:11,533 --> 00:22:14,567
- Okay, Ma'am. We'll go ahead.
- Be careful, okay?

345
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:15,967
Thank you.

346
00:22:21,133 --> 00:22:22,200
Mom...

347
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:24,133
- Joey?
- Look at this.

348
00:22:28,467 --> 00:22:31,100
I saw it on the sleeve
of Godfather Diego's jacket.

349
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,533
What am I going to do with it?

350
00:22:34,667 --> 00:22:38,800
Mother, I think that's where
the evidence I'm looking for is.

351
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,633
That's why he put it there.

352
00:22:42,767 --> 00:22:44,167
Why did you just tell me now?

353
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:46,467
Let's go after the Chief!
Let's give it to him!

354
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,333
- What?
- No Mom.

355
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:49,667
I've learned my lesson.

356
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:53,167
We need to see what's inside
before we surrender it.

357
00:23:07,867 --> 00:23:09,133
Tomas, Clarissa.

358
00:23:09,267 --> 00:23:10,800
I don't want to bother you
anymore.

359
00:23:10,933 --> 00:23:13,267
There's new evidence
that just came out.

360
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,433
What evidence?

361
00:23:14,567 --> 00:23:16,867
I'm working on a way
to find Theresa.

362
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,700
I'm hoping that it pays off
this time.

363
00:23:18,833 --> 00:23:22,800
Delgado got some new evidence.
Find out right away what it is.

364
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:24,800
The question now, Ka-Tiradas,

365
00:23:24,933 --> 00:23:28,500
is what will happen in the case
of Major Miguel Delgado,

366
00:23:28,633 --> 00:23:32,033
who was first accused
of killing Ramon Orbos?

367
00:23:32,167 --> 00:23:34,200
Andrew knows a lot
about Delgado.

368
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:35,433
What, Berdugo?

369
00:23:35,567 --> 00:23:37,700
Should I include him in
what I'm cooking for Delgado?

370
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:40,200
Because of the evidence
that came out

371
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:42,700
in the case of Major
Miguel Delgado,

372
00:23:42,833 --> 00:23:46,500
the court has already made
a decision, Ka-Tiradas.
